From: awto-tl-st1008f
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: rtl83xx: l3: route on a non-switch upper is CPU-trapped by design, not an error (#124)

A route directly on a standalone DSA port (OpenWrt preinit 192.168.1.1/24 on lan1) has only the
conduit below it, so otto_l3_port_dev_lower_find() finds no port and the route is trapped to
the CPU, as the comment above it intends. Log at debug and return 0 (no "fib_add() failed").
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/rtl83xx/l3.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/rtl83xx/l3.c
@@ -2779,9 +2779,9 @@
 	 */
 	port = otto_l3_port_dev_lower_find(ndev, ctrl);
 	if (port < 0) {
-		dev_err(ctrl->dev, "lower interface %s not found\n", ndev->name);
+		dev_dbg(ctrl->dev, "route on %s: no switch port below, CPU-trapped\n", ndev->name);
 		otto_l3_fib_trap_v4(ctrl, info);
-		return -ENODEV;
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	/* Allocate route or host-route entry (if hardware supports this) */
